        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(slack): preserve interaction thread status",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Preserve Slack block-action thread context from `message.thread_ts` when `container.thread_ts` is absent.\n- Add Slack heartbeat typing and clear-typing support by updating Slack assistant thread status for thread-targeted follow-up turns.\n- Cover the interaction delivery context and heartbeat status adapter with focused Slack tests.\n\n## Verification\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/slack/src/monitor/events/interactions.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/slack/src/channel.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/outbound/targets.test.ts`\n\n## Real behavior proof\nBehavior addressed: Slack interactive reply follow-up turns retain their thread context and can show and clear native assistant thread status while the agent is working.\n\nReal environment tested: Local OpenClaw source checkout on macOS, using the patched Slack channel and interaction event code in this branch.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch: Ran the local OpenClaw verification commands below after applying the patch.\n\nEvidence after fix: Terminal capture from the local OpenClaw checkout:\n\n```text\n$ git diff --check\n(no output)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/slack/src/monitor/events/interactions.test.ts\n(exit 0)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/slack/src/channel.test.ts\n(exit 0)\n\n$ node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/outbound/targets.test.ts\n(exit 0)\n```\n\nObserved result after fix: The interaction event path now carries the fallback Slack thread timestamp into `threadTs`, session-key resolution, and `deliveryContext.threadId`; the Slack heartbeat adapter now sends `assistant.threads.setStatus` with `is typing...` and clears it with an empty status for a threaded Slack target. The local commands above completed successfully.\n\nWhat was not tested: A live Slack socket-mode workspace and a real Slack assistant thread.\n\nFixes #82886\n",
